    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate leaning heavily into speed and favorable park factors, anchored by our strongest play, **Tyler Soderstrom** (74.75). Despite the challenge of facing Freddy Peralta, **Tyler Soderstrom** benefits from a massive 10% park boost and a high-leverage cleanup spot, positioning him to maximize counting stats. Similarly, **Corbin Carroll** (73.48) is a must-start; the dynamic platoon advantage against Gabriel Hughes is statistically significant, and his elite sprint speed remains our primary weapon to maintain a lead in the SB category. **Isaac Paredes** (63.56) and **Mickey Moniak** (61.43) round out the top tier, with **Mickey Moniak**\u2019s massive +14% platoon adjustment against Michael Soroka making him a high-efficiency pivot despite his typical secondary status in the outfield rotation.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today involves balancing the volatility of the bottom-order hitters against our limited game caps. While **Austin Riley** (48.94) is technically a start, his low score\u2014compounded by a 31% rain risk\u2014puts him on the edge of the \"marginal\" threshold. He holds the spot primarily due to a lack of viable alternatives on our bench, as **Josh Naylor** and **Jose Caballero** are inactive today, and both **James Wood** and **Vinnie Pasquantino** remain sidelined on the IL. We are closely monitoring the lineups for **Gabriel Moreno** and **Brice Turang**; if either falls out of the top three spots in their respective orders, their efficiency scores will drop, potentially forcing a defensive shuffle to protect our cap usage. \n\nWe are also proceeding with caution regarding **Max Muncy** (54.98), who is currently slotted into a difficult matchup against Freddy Peralta. While the park boost is helpful, the -6% penalty for batting eighth is a drag on his potential. As we navigate the day, we remain optimistic that the projected output from **Henry Bolte** (61.02), who thrives at the top of the order with a +10% placement boost, will mitigate the risk of our lower-scoring infield assets. We continue to hold prospects like **Dalton Rushing**, **Zach McKinstry**, **Cole Young**, **Edwin Arroyo**, and **Travis Bazzana** in reserve, alongside veterans **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Seiya Suzuki**, and **Trevor Story**, ready to rotate if the early game reports suggest a collapse in lineup positioning.",
